{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 86, :comments ["<b>Twelve gold pans.</b> Why is this stated? Since it says ״כַּף אַחַת עֲשָׂרָה זָהָב״ — perhaps it was of gold and its weight was ten shekels of silver, or perhaps it was one pan of silver and its weight was ten shekels of gold — and the weight of gold shekels is not equal to that of silver — therefore Scripture says ״כַּפּוֹת זָהָב״ — they were of gold (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:53.420269826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}